# Recommended additions to your project's own .gitignore after installing OctoCheck.
# These are working files regenerated on every run — not useful to commit, and
# progress.json in particular can churn on every single task, creating merge noise.

octocheck/cache/
octocheck/progress.json

# octocheck/plan.md and octocheck/reports/ are usually worth committing — plan.md
# documents what a review covered, and reports/ is the actual review history over
# time. Remove the two lines above if you'd rather keep everything, e.g. to inspect
# cache/progress state in CI logs.
